1
00:00:05,080 --> 00:00:06,600
Isn't that P'Big Jane?

2
00:00:07,160 --> 00:00:08,680
I'm sorry for everything.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:10,400
You are my new dream.

4
00:00:11,040 --> 00:00:12,240
Will you marry me?

5
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:14,320
Sure.

6
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,640
Jane, stay with me!

7
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,479
Jane, wake up and talk to me first.

8
00:00:32,479 --> 00:00:34,360
I'd give up anything for you, Jane.

9
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:36,920
Who are you?

10
00:00:37,160 --> 00:00:38,520
The condition Jane is experiencing

11
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:41,320
a state where a patient loses memories

12
00:00:41,320 --> 00:00:43,360
due to brain trauma.

13
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:44,280
He can only remember

14
00:00:44,280 --> 00:00:47,120
before he started his second year of university.

15
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:49,840
Then you probably don't remember

16
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:52,880
that we were seeing each other for a while?

17
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:54,920
If you still can't remember me...

18
00:00:54,920 --> 00:00:57,800
I will make you fall in love with me all over again.

19
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:16,000
How are you?

20
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:17,720
Huh.

21
00:01:19,039 --> 00:01:20,320
I'm ok mom.

22
00:01:22,800 --> 00:01:23,520
But...

23
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:26,720
Why is our home...

24
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:30,600
You sold the house to him.

25
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,720
Why?

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,440
I was the one who caused trouble.

27
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,920
I got our family into ten million baht of debt.

28
00:01:57,560 --> 00:01:59,360
P'Jane helped by buying the house

29
00:01:59,360 --> 00:02:01,040
and giving me the money to pay off the debt.

30
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,480
If he wanted to help,

31
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:06,880
why did he have to kick you out of the house?

32
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:09,639
Why did he make your family

33
00:02:09,639 --> 00:02:11,600
have to live in a place as rundown as this?

34
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:13,000
I will buy this house...

35
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,240
I didn't kick them out.

36
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,960
Jane was the one who decided to move out on his own.

37
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:17,120
I don't believe you.

38
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:19,200
Why would Jane do something like that?

39
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:20,600
Ah!

40
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:22,400
Ouch!

41
00:02:23,079 --> 00:02:23,880
Stop!

42
00:02:25,079 --> 00:02:25,640
Jane?

43
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:26,760
Jane!

44
00:02:28,440 --> 00:02:29,040
Ah!

45
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:30,160
Jane!

46
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:32,000
Jane!

47
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:35,600
Are you alright?

48
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,320
Jane is probably exhausted now.

49
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,200
You should head back first.

50
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:17,280
In that case, I'll take my leave.

51
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:23,800
Goodbye, P'Jane.

52
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:03,800
You walk in with a warning sign

53
00:04:06,160 --> 00:04:11,240
Just one look and already falling for you

54
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:18,360
My friends tell me not to cross that line

55
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:25,640
But I’m already out of time

56
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:29,720
I know the truth, I taste the sin

57
00:04:29,720 --> 00:04:31,320
It’s wrong but I don’t want it to be true

58
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,840
I’m losing all my discipline

59
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:38,000
You’re all I’m thinking of

60
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,080
and I’m breaking all the rules

61
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:42,360
just because…

62
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:45,760
You’re a red flag but I’m colorblind

63
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:49,159
I know you’re dangerous

64
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,960
If it burns, let it burn me alive

65
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:57,280
I can't hold myself back, I’d cross every line

66
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:05,560
Ooh

67
00:05:20,840 --> 00:05:21,720
When it comes to treatment,

68
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:23,600
I've done everything I can.

69
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,920
Does that mean

70
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,200
Little Jane will have to be like this forever?

71
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,920
It's not like that.

72
00:05:32,440 --> 00:05:33,920
I just want you to take it easy.

73
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,800
With cases like this, sometimes it takes months,

74
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,880
and for some, it takes over a year

75
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:39,880
for all their memories to return.

76
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,520
But I can't take this anymore.

77
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:46,200
Isn't there any way to make

78
00:05:46,200 --> 00:05:48,200
Little Jane remember faster?

79
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:57,680
To be honest, there is a way.

80
00:05:58,200 --> 00:05:59,159
Maybe..

81
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:03,040
you might need to take him to places,

82
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,640
events,

83
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,560
or meet people associated with the memories he forgot.

84
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:09,360
Who knows, doing something like this

85
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:11,760
might make his memories come back faster.

86
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,760
But let me warn you about one thing,

87
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:17,560
I can't guarantee how that goes.

88
00:06:19,040 --> 00:06:21,560
For some people, doing this

89
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,680
might cause them to go into shock,

90
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,680
or they might not be able to accept

91
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,400
the self that they had forgotten.

92
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,360
Either way...

93
00:06:31,840 --> 00:06:33,840
just take it slow and start gently first.

94
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,440
I had no idea

95
00:07:05,920 --> 00:07:07,200
you liked taking photos, P'Dan.

96
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:11,240
You ask just like back in our university days,

97
00:07:11,520 --> 00:07:12,640
back when

98
00:07:12,640 --> 00:07:14,800
you came to help me out at the academic fair.

99
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:17,560
Really?

100
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:25,240
I'm sorry...

101
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:28,080
that I can't remember.

102
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:30,360
Why are you apologizing to me?

103
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:31,680
Well...

104
00:07:32,280 --> 00:07:33,680
for you,

105
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,680
it feels like it haven't happened yet, right?

106
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:41,800
Let me take a photo of you.

107
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:44,520
Why?

108
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:47,960
Come on, I won't sell it like last time.

109
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,320
What did you say?

110
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:53,080
Nothing!

111
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:54,720
Come on.

112
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:56,120
Give it a try.

113
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:58,080
One, two...

114
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,080
Ooh,

115
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:01,600
looks nice!

116
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:05,000
This one...

117
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:06,920
Whoa...

118
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,280
Hey.

119
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,680
Do I really look that old, P'Dan?

120
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:14,920
Mm...

121
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,240
Suddenly having five years added to your age

122
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,440
without realizing it,

123
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,720
it probably feels something like this.

124
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,560
But if you ask me,

125
00:08:22,280 --> 00:08:23,720
you're still not as old as I am.

126
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:25,000
Hahaha!

127
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:27,400
Let me get one more shot,

128
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,200
a redo.

129
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:29,440
Let's try again.

130
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,400
One, two...

131
00:08:38,320 --> 00:08:39,200
(Mr. Jane Patrick Terry Palakorn)

132
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:46,160
So is there something you want to tell me about?

133
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,600
About your age?

134
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,880
And about Harvard?

135
00:08:51,320 --> 00:08:51,840
Uh...

136
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:52,760
Jane,

137
00:08:53,560 --> 00:08:54,520
are you alright?

138
00:09:03,520 --> 00:09:04,320
I'm fine.

139
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:22,320
Jane, I think

140
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:23,720
this angle looks great.

141
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,320
Let's take a selfie together.

142
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,600
Here we go.

143
00:09:29,240 --> 00:09:30,400
One, two...

144
00:09:35,120 --> 00:09:36,160
Look at the camera.

145
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:39,360
The background looks nice, see?

146
00:09:41,040 --> 00:09:41,960
Are you okay?

147
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,760
I'm okay.

148
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:44,520
One more photo.

149
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,600
One, two...

150
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:48,120
Here.

151
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:52,520
You don't look old, see?

152
00:09:53,560 --> 00:09:54,360
Whoa...

153
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:55,920
Here.

154
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,600
What are you guys doing?

155
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:19,920
Getting ready to live stream selling herbs.

156
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:21,800
There's this much of it?

157
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,080
Yeah.

158
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:25,160
It's really trending right now.

159
00:10:25,160 --> 00:10:27,040
And those herbal sachets you came up with,

160
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:28,320
they are super popular.

161
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:36,520
Jane.

162
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,400
I'll get the door.

163
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:46,240
Is there anything I can help with, Jean?

164
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,680
Hello, P'Jane.

165
00:10:48,120 --> 00:10:49,240
Come on in.

166
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,760
Hello, P'Jane.

167
00:10:58,320 --> 00:10:59,000
Hello.

168
00:11:07,440 --> 00:11:09,040
Hello uncle and auntie.

169
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,160
Hi.

170
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:12,760
Hello.

171
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:16,360
I'm coming to ask for permission

172
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,080
to take Jane to my place today.

173
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,240
I'm not letting him go.

174
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,200
Calm down first.

175
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,920
Well, I'm just worried that something

176
00:11:24,920 --> 00:11:26,400
might happen to Jane again.

177
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,120
I feel the same way.

178
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:30,040
And I think that right now,

179
00:11:30,720 --> 00:11:32,080
he shouldn't go anywhere.

180
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,640
But I've already consulted with P'Ram

181
00:11:34,880 --> 00:11:36,120
regarding Jane's condition.

182
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:38,280
P'Ram said

183
00:11:38,800 --> 00:11:40,040
that if Jane encounters situations

184
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:42,280
or people from the period he forgot,

185
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:45,920
it might help trigger his memories to come back.

186
00:11:47,600 --> 00:11:48,240
So that's why you came

187
00:11:48,240 --> 00:11:50,000
to pick my brother up, right, P'Jane?

188
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:52,480
Yes.

189
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:54,920
Besides,

190
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,360
there's someone I want Jane to meet.

191
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,640
It's up to you, Jane.

192
00:12:11,640 --> 00:12:13,400
If you're not ready yet, it's okay.

193
00:12:21,800 --> 00:12:23,120
Teach me.

194
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,720
I want to draw a race car.

195
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:41,600
I want to go.

196
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,000
Jane...

197
00:12:45,520 --> 00:12:46,200
Jane...

198
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:48,600
We're worried about you, you know?

199
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:53,160
But it's the only way that can help Jane, you know.

200
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,800
You should know

201
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,880
that we...

202
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:08,320
As for the person who crashed into the car last time,

203
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:09,760
I currently have a police acquaintance

204
00:13:09,760 --> 00:13:11,160
looking into it.

205
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:12,960
It won't be long,

206
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:15,160
we should be able to identify the person behind it.

207
00:13:19,800 --> 00:13:22,160
Don't you want Jane to regain his memories?

208
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,640
Please?

209
00:13:26,040 --> 00:13:27,560
Please let him go.

210
00:13:28,160 --> 00:13:29,640
I can tell

211
00:13:30,120 --> 00:13:31,360
that my brother doesn't want to stay

212
00:13:31,360 --> 00:13:33,120
like this forever either.

213
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:39,920
Please?

214
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,760
I don't want to be a burden to everyone.

215
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:46,160
I want to remember everything again.

216
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,040
We're here, this is my house...

217
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,520
the house we used to live in together.

218
00:14:58,400 --> 00:14:59,240
Hello,

219
00:14:59,440 --> 00:15:00,520
Mr. Little Jane.

220
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:03,400
Hello.

221
00:15:04,840 --> 00:15:05,920
You are...

222
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,360
It's Auntie May.

223
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:11,800
It's so wonderful to have you back.

224
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,280
Ever since you left,

225
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:17,040
Mr.Jane hasn't seemed lively at all.

226
00:15:23,640 --> 00:15:25,000
Where is Jamie, Auntie May?

227
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,400
He's upstairs.

228
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:28,200
He'll be down in a moment.

229
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,760
In that case, I'll go call him down, okay?

230
00:15:33,360 --> 00:15:34,160
Sure.

231
00:15:46,520 --> 00:15:47,360
Jane...

232
00:15:51,280 --> 00:15:52,200
Did you know

233
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:54,120
where the dining room was?

234
00:15:56,680 --> 00:15:58,080
I didn't know.

235
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:01,320
I just felt like...

236
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:03,160
it had to be this way.

237
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:12,680
Lil' Jane...

238
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:31,880
Do you remember...

239
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,200
me?

240
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,200
Jane...

241
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,560
Jane? Do you remember Jamie?

242
00:18:02,240 --> 00:18:03,640
I don't remember yet,

243
00:18:05,480 --> 00:18:06,800
but I can really feel it..

244
00:18:07,600 --> 00:18:10,440
that you must be someone very important.

245
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:01,560
You draw so well.

246
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,200
That's because Lil' Jane is a good teacher!

247
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,600
Then will you teach me again?

248
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:10,320
Of course.

249
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,840
How about we draw a bird?

250
00:19:14,200 --> 00:19:15,080
Sure.

251
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:17,440
Then...

252
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:20,000
let's start with the outline first,

253
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,480
and then draw the face.

254
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:01,640
I'm sorry...

255
00:20:02,400 --> 00:20:03,960
that I still can't remember.

256
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:06,320
Why are you apologizing?

257
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:10,120
It's not your fault at all.

258
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,360
I'm just happy

259
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,400
to see you bright and lively while drawing again.

260
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:20,520
It reminds me of you back in university.

261
00:20:22,800 --> 00:20:23,360
Well...

262
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:26,080
I am still in university.

263
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,400
That's true.

264
00:20:31,440 --> 00:20:32,440
So...

265
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,600
what was I like when I was working?

266
00:20:37,960 --> 00:20:40,520
When you worked, you looked quite happy.

267
00:20:41,160 --> 00:20:42,920
Probably because you were close to me.

268
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:46,920
Though you still couldn't say no

269
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,920
to other people as usual.

270
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:50,520
Well...

271
00:20:51,040 --> 00:20:52,400
sounds just like me.

272
00:21:06,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Come over here.

273
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:09,120
There's something I want to show you.

274
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,320
Jane?

275
00:21:54,400 --> 00:21:55,400
Is something wrong?

276
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:04,920
Jane?

277
00:22:07,760 --> 00:22:08,440
Jane?

278
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:10,800
Are you okay?

279
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:14,280
Jane?

280
00:22:15,360 --> 00:22:16,400
Let go of me!

281
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:46,680
Gap,

282
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:48,440
explain to me why I had to wear

283
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,600
a student uniform too?

284
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,360
I look too old for this!

285
00:22:51,360 --> 00:22:52,920
And Khing didn't even show up!

286
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:54,800
Stop complaining.

287
00:22:55,160 --> 00:22:57,720
It's to help bring back Jane's memories.

288
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,360
Just help out.

289
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:01,120
You still look good though.

290
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:02,760
Yeah.

291
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,600
Yeah, Jane, so how are you doing?

292
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:10,800
Thanks a lot, guys,

293
00:23:11,200 --> 00:23:12,160
for doing all this for me.

294
00:23:14,920 --> 00:23:16,760
I'm going to invite P'Big Jane over too.

295
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,040
He should be here soon.

296
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:23,200
I really want to know...

297
00:23:23,840 --> 00:23:25,320
am I actually dating P'Jane?

298
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:27,080
Can you tell me about

299
00:23:27,080 --> 00:23:28,400
back when we first started dating?

300
00:23:29,400 --> 00:23:30,200
Sure.

301
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:32,800
Though we don't know a whole lot, to be honest.

302
00:23:33,120 --> 00:23:34,320
From what we saw,

303
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:37,200
you and P'Jane took a bunch of classes together,

304
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,240
so you two became really close.

305
00:23:39,520 --> 00:23:40,400
And P'Dan?

306
00:23:41,200 --> 00:23:42,160
P'Dan

307
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:43,280
came along right around the time

308
00:23:43,280 --> 00:23:44,960
you and P'Jane took a break.

309
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:45,920
But that was super brief,

310
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:46,920
you dumped him

311
00:23:47,240 --> 00:23:48,480
and went right back to P'Jane.

312
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:49,720
Holy crap...

313
00:23:51,600 --> 00:23:52,840
did I really do all that?

314
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,160
And...

315
00:23:59,120 --> 00:24:00,600
what was P'Jane like

316
00:24:05,320 --> 00:24:06,560
back in our university days?

317
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:09,720
Not many people dared to mess with him, honestly.

318
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:11,080
Yeah, for real.

319
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:12,360
And there were always weird rumors

320
00:24:12,360 --> 00:24:13,520
going around about him,

321
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:14,720
like...

322
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:16,960
like he was some kind of demon or something,

323
00:24:17,360 --> 00:24:18,120
where you could make a contract

324
00:24:18,120 --> 00:24:19,480
to ask for anything,

325
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:22,680
but when he came to collect the debt,

326
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:25,720
your life could get completely ruined, you know?

327
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:27,240
Why are you saying things that'll make him

328
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,600
scared of P'Jane?

329
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,160
My boss takes exceptionally good care of him, okay?

330
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,320
Gosh, look at you, so devoted to your boss!

331
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:34,080
Well!

332
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:36,400
Of course! He's a good person!

333
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:37,840
Back in our uni days,

334
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,040
Put was trying so hard

335
00:24:39,040 --> 00:24:40,960
to keep P'Jane away from Jane.

336
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:44,600
Oh, yeah!

337
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:45,720
Speaking of Put,

338
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,280
I haven't seen him at all since I woke up.

339
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:54,360
Where did he go?

340
00:24:57,040 --> 00:24:57,840
Well...

341
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:02,400
Oops!

342
00:25:02,760 --> 00:25:03,720
Holy shit! Uh...

343
00:25:03,720 --> 00:25:04,280
Hey!!

344
00:25:04,520 --> 00:25:05,640
Huh?

345
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:06,320
That was a miss.

346
00:25:06,520 --> 00:25:07,560
Gap, what the hell are you doing?

347
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:08,920
Guess my aim is off today.

348
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:09,800
My feet are getting tired.

349
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:11,160
Could you go get that for me?

350
00:25:11,320 --> 00:25:11,960
Please? I'm...

351
00:25:11,960 --> 00:25:13,120
Yeah, I'm exhausted.

352
00:25:14,720 --> 00:25:16,400
Please, please go pick it up for me!

353
00:25:16,960 --> 00:25:18,000
Go get it for me, please!

354
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:19,000
Alright, alright.

355
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:20,200
You're the sweetest!

356
00:25:41,080 --> 00:25:42,520
Can I have the ball back, please?

357
00:26:09,080 --> 00:26:10,120
Can I have the ball back, please,

358
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,600
so we can keep playing.

359
00:26:28,400 --> 00:26:29,000
Jane,

360
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,720
I'm sorry

361
00:26:32,160 --> 00:26:33,560
about what happened at my house yesterday.

362
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:36,280
I didn't mean to make you feel bad.

363
00:26:38,360 --> 00:26:40,520
I'm sorry too, P'Jane,

364
00:26:42,400 --> 00:26:44,120
for not listening to you at all...

365
00:26:47,000 --> 00:26:49,760
even though you were just trying to help me.

366
00:26:52,120 --> 00:26:53,320
It was my fault.

367
00:26:54,200 --> 00:26:55,280
Honestly,

368
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:59,000
I should have started with something small first.

369
00:27:05,920 --> 00:27:06,680
So...

370
00:27:07,160 --> 00:27:08,800
what should we start with today?

371
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:11,720
Back in uni,

372
00:27:12,840 --> 00:27:14,040
we used to sit and write reports

373
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,560
together at this table.

374
00:27:17,800 --> 00:27:19,360
This was our usual spot.

375
00:27:22,160 --> 00:27:22,960
Really?

376
00:28:01,400 --> 00:28:02,640
What are you doing?

377
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:27,520
Are you cold?

378
00:28:33,640 --> 00:28:34,680
Do you remember, Jane?

379
00:29:05,760 --> 00:29:06,840
Whoa!

380
00:29:10,360 --> 00:29:11,160
Gap!

381
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:12,600
Fahsai!

382
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:14,520
Salmon!

383
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:15,800
Pai!

384
00:29:17,920 --> 00:29:18,760
Damn.

385
00:29:20,400 --> 00:29:22,200
P'Jane really went all out.

386
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,080
Whoa.

387
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:25,440
Hey.

388
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:26,640
Loma.

389
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:27,800
First.

390
00:29:29,640 --> 00:29:30,600
Long time no see!

391
00:29:30,960 --> 00:29:31,760
Oops!

392
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,440
Oops!

393
00:29:34,600 --> 00:29:37,120
How are you doing, Little Jane?

394
00:29:37,320 --> 00:29:39,000
Still as tiny as ever!

395
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:39,760
Ouch!

396
00:29:39,760 --> 00:29:40,960
Doing well, right?

397
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:42,880
Little Jane?

398
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:43,800
Yes! Little Jane!

399
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:46,320
Just listen and go along with it dude,

400
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:47,400
you'll understand soon.

401
00:29:48,320 --> 00:29:50,640
Professor, don't go spoiling it just yet.

402
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:52,000
Oh! Oops!

403
00:29:52,200 --> 00:29:52,720
Owh!

404
00:29:53,120 --> 00:29:54,400
Babes!

405
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:56,000
Let's take attendance now, shall we?

406
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,400
Come gather around everyone!

407
00:29:58,400 --> 00:29:59,840
Let's start class.

408
00:30:03,240 --> 00:30:05,040
You're Jennalee, right?

409
00:30:05,320 --> 00:30:05,800
Yes.

410
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:08,600
In the last class, you took sick leave,

411
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:10,680
so I had everyone pair up,

412
00:30:10,680 --> 00:30:12,600
and everyone is taken already.

413
00:30:12,600 --> 00:30:14,080
But that's totally fine.

414
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:16,560
We have another special student

415
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:18,840
joining us for their first day today as well.

416
00:30:32,280 --> 00:30:34,200
There's your dance partner.

417
00:30:34,720 --> 00:30:36,800
Jane Patrick.

418
00:31:03,880 --> 00:31:04,760
Ahem!

419
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,480
Okay, everyone!

420
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:08,040
Um,

421
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:09,600
you're... uh...

422
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:11,440
Jennalee, right?

423
00:31:11,440 --> 00:31:12,800
And you are Jane Patrick.

424
00:31:12,800 --> 00:31:13,520
Oh!

425
00:31:13,520 --> 00:31:15,640
You have the same name.

426
00:31:15,640 --> 00:31:17,800
I'll just give you a new nickname.

427
00:31:17,800 --> 00:31:19,160
so it's easier for me to call you.

428
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:22,200
You're still as tiny as ever,

429
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:23,720
so let's call you Little Jane, okay?

430
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:24,320
As for you...

431
00:31:24,320 --> 00:31:26,600
gosh, you're still as big and tall as ever!

432
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:29,800
Ah, I'll call you Big Jane  then.

433
00:31:29,800 --> 00:31:31,800
Little Jane will dance as the lady,

434
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:33,400
and Big Jane as the gentleman.

435
00:31:33,400 --> 00:31:34,840
Hahaha, tiny one!

436
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:37,200
Little one, little one!

437
00:31:37,200 --> 00:31:38,720
Alright, pair up now!

438
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:39,360
Pair up! Gap!

439
00:31:39,360 --> 00:31:40,640
Turn to your partner!

440
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:49,840
May I dance with you?

441
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:12,200
Alright, I'm going to start counting the rhythm now.

442
00:32:12,520 --> 00:32:14,200
Take it nice and easy.

443
00:32:14,400 --> 00:32:15,000
Count...

444
00:32:15,320 --> 00:32:18,040
One, two, three, go!

445
00:32:18,480 --> 00:32:21,080
One, two, three...

446
00:32:21,440 --> 00:32:23,920
One, two, three...

447
00:32:24,760 --> 00:32:27,000
Very good! Keep going!

448
00:32:30,600 --> 00:32:31,920
Do you remember anything at all?

449
00:32:33,720 --> 00:32:34,880
I still don't remember...

450
00:32:39,320 --> 00:32:39,880
but...

451
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:44,520
it feels like my body is just moving on its own.

452
00:32:50,080 --> 00:32:52,960
Alright, everyone, get ready to turn!

453
00:32:55,200 --> 00:32:56,680
When you turn, remember to shift

454
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:58,880
your weight onto the other leg.

455
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,080
This is the condo where we lived

456
00:33:37,080 --> 00:33:39,320
together during university.

457
00:33:40,440 --> 00:33:41,920
It's this luxurious?

458
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:39,280
I'm sorry, P'Jane...

459
00:34:40,360 --> 00:34:41,159
um...

460
00:34:41,840 --> 00:34:43,560
I don't like eating ginkgo nuts.

461
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:45,360
I know.

462
00:34:46,880 --> 00:34:48,480
But try just one bite.

463
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:51,320
I put my all into making it.

464
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:55,040
It's not bitter at all.

465
00:35:37,920 --> 00:35:39,320
How did you do that, P'Jane?

466
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,520
I knew

467
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,520
you disliked them because of the bitter taste,

468
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:48,560
so I secretly went and found a way

469
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:50,200
to make them easy for you to eat.

470
00:35:54,320 --> 00:35:55,200
Thank you.

471
00:35:58,200 --> 00:35:59,240
I have one more thing...

472
00:36:13,320 --> 00:36:14,720
Please have some cake with me.

473
00:36:16,960 --> 00:36:18,600
Today happens to be my birthday.

474
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:24,680
Today is your birthday, P'Jane?

475
00:36:26,440 --> 00:36:27,720
I'm so sorry...

476
00:36:28,040 --> 00:36:29,560
that I didn't remember.

477
00:36:33,240 --> 00:36:34,040
It's alright.

478
00:36:35,760 --> 00:36:37,320
How could I ever be angry with you?

479
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:43,040
Happy birthday, P'Jane.

480
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:49,440
Is there anything you want for your birthday?

481
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,120
I want you.

482
00:36:58,760 --> 00:36:59,560
Uh...

483
00:36:59,880 --> 00:37:01,840
I want my old Jane back.

484
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:22,040
It's okay, Jane.

485
00:37:24,760 --> 00:37:26,400
It doesn't matter if you still can't remember.

486
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:30,120
I'll always be right here with you.

487
00:38:25,600 --> 00:38:27,400
You play the piano so well, P'Jane.

488
00:38:31,160 --> 00:38:32,640
You once asked me

489
00:38:33,600 --> 00:38:35,400
if I didn't run a business

490
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:38,800
what my dream would be.

491
00:38:40,080 --> 00:38:41,520
So I told you

492
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:43,320
that when I was a kid,

493
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:47,080
I dreamt of becoming a pianist.

494
00:38:59,160 --> 00:39:00,280
Want to give it a try?

495
00:39:04,600 --> 00:39:05,560
I don't know how to play.

496
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:05,520
Ah.

497
00:40:07,120 --> 00:40:07,920
P'Jane.

498
00:40:32,720 --> 00:40:35,120
Before you lost your memory,

499
00:40:39,240 --> 00:40:40,800
we promised each other that...

500
00:40:44,040 --> 00:40:45,360
we were going to get married.

501
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,480
I'll wait for you, Jane.

502
00:40:56,120 --> 00:40:57,920
What if you have to wait forever?

503
00:40:59,680 --> 00:41:01,120
Even if it's forever, I'll still wait.

504
00:41:05,720 --> 00:41:07,680
But I don't want to hold you back.

505
00:41:09,280 --> 00:41:10,520
I'm in so much pain.

506
00:41:11,800 --> 00:41:13,080
I feel so guilty that...

507
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:15,920
I can't remember anything at all..

508
00:41:16,760 --> 00:41:19,240
that I couldn't even remember your special day...

509
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:23,440
I don't even remember

510
00:41:24,200 --> 00:41:25,720
how we fell in love.

511
00:41:30,800 --> 00:41:31,600
How am I supposed to be a good partner

512
00:41:31,600 --> 00:41:32,800
to you like this?

513
00:41:41,280 --> 00:41:42,440
And I'm scared...

514
00:41:43,480 --> 00:41:46,120
None of this feels like my life at all.

515
00:41:58,000 --> 00:41:59,160
I'd give anything.

516
00:42:01,840 --> 00:42:02,760
Just please...

517
00:42:05,200 --> 00:42:06,880
Jane, don't leave me.

518
00:42:08,480 --> 00:42:10,360
I'm willing to give up everything I have.

519
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:12,920
I can even stop running favors.

520
00:42:18,560 --> 00:42:20,280
Can you just stay with me for now?

521
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,600
I'm sorry...

522
00:42:57,000 --> 00:42:57,720
Jane.

523
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:03,040
When you said you loved me,

524
00:43:03,040 --> 00:43:06,800
or were you just saying it?

525
00:43:06,800 --> 00:43:10,560
Because what you did makes it so clear

526
00:43:10,560 --> 00:43:12,160
You tricked me into loving you,

527
00:43:12,160 --> 00:43:15,600
and then you destroyed me

528
00:43:15,600 --> 00:43:18,400
You said you loved me,

529
00:43:18,400 --> 00:43:22,080
yet you hurt me

530
00:43:22,080 --> 00:43:25,600
The more I love you,

531
00:43:25,600 --> 00:43:27,800
the more it hurts

532
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:30,240
I just want to know,

533
00:43:30,240 --> 00:43:33,240
did you ever love me?

534
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:40,760
Jane.

535
00:43:43,040 --> 00:43:43,840
P'Dan?

536
00:43:45,000 --> 00:43:45,920
How did you get here?

537
00:43:46,600 --> 00:43:48,080
I went to your apartment.

538
00:43:48,920 --> 00:43:50,480
Your mom said you were here.

539
00:43:52,240 --> 00:43:53,680
Did he do something to you?

540
00:43:57,000 --> 00:43:57,800
Want to go home?

541
00:43:59,280 --> 00:44:00,240
I'll can take you home.

542
00:44:08,000 --> 00:44:09,640
I won't let Jane go anywhere.

543
00:44:17,400 --> 00:44:18,640
Jane wants to leave.

544
00:44:20,280 --> 00:44:21,440
Stop forcing him.

545
00:44:21,760 --> 00:44:22,840
Then stop sticking your nose

546
00:44:22,840 --> 00:44:24,080
into my business with Jane.

547
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:25,960
This is one thing I have to butt into.

548
00:44:26,600 --> 00:44:27,680
I won't let Jane stay anywhere near

549
00:44:27,680 --> 00:44:28,920
a dangerous person like you.

550
00:44:29,800 --> 00:44:31,200
Don't make me repeat myself.

551
00:44:32,400 --> 00:44:33,560
Is that a threat?

552
00:44:35,560 --> 00:44:37,440
You threatened Put the exact same way, didn't you?

553
00:44:37,920 --> 00:44:38,840
Put?

554
00:44:41,600 --> 00:44:42,520
What happened?

555
00:44:43,760 --> 00:44:44,360
Jane.

556
00:44:45,560 --> 00:44:46,680
Jane, stay calm.

557
00:44:47,080 --> 00:44:48,720
But I really have to tell you this

558
00:44:49,960 --> 00:44:51,720
so you'll stop getting involved with him for good.

559
00:44:56,280 --> 00:44:56,760
Put is...

560
00:44:57,200 --> 00:44:57,720
Hey.

561
00:44:57,920 --> 00:44:58,560
Hey!

562
00:45:00,840 --> 00:45:01,640
Stop!

563
00:45:02,680 --> 00:45:03,800
Stop!! Jane, don't listen to him!

564
00:45:04,040 --> 00:45:05,400
I can explain this!

565
00:45:05,600 --> 00:45:06,400
Stop!

566
00:45:09,120 --> 00:45:09,920
P'Dan!

567
00:45:11,080 --> 00:45:11,800
Speak!

568
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:14,480
Put is dead

569
00:45:16,520 --> 00:45:17,440
and he is

570
00:45:17,760 --> 00:45:19,920
the one behind Put's death!

571
00:45:21,920 --> 00:45:23,360
You told me yourself.

572
00:45:23,800 --> 00:45:24,600
It's not true.

573
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:26,960
Jane, you know I didn't do it.

574
00:46:28,400 --> 00:46:28,880
Jane!

575
00:46:32,120 --> 00:46:32,640
Go!

576
00:46:32,640 --> 00:46:34,040
Jane!

577
00:46:34,040 --> 00:46:34,560
Don't...

578
00:46:41,920 --> 00:46:42,440
Jane!

579
00:46:43,960 --> 00:46:44,760
Jane!

580
00:47:39,200 --> 00:47:42,480
(P'Dan)

581
00:49:37,560 --> 00:49:38,520
To P'Jane,

582
00:49:39,360 --> 00:49:41,920
I've read the letter you left for me.

583
